{"title":"SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? (TechCrunch, 2023-10-01T14:00:29+00:00)","text":"SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? (TechCrunch, 2023-10-01T14:00:29+00:00)
Within two years, more than 80 investors provided about $2 billion in capital to FTX, helping Bankman-Fried propel his vision into a reality. In January 2022, the company raised $400 million in a Series C round, boosting its valuation to $32 billion. That was its last round of public funding.

The company gained somewhat mainstream recognition with branding deals and partnerships. For example, in 2021 it bought the naming rights for the Miami Heat’s home arena. FTX also got its name branded on Major League Baseball umpires’ polos, and it partnered with celebrities like Tom Brady and his ex-wife, Gisele Bündchen, as well as Steph Curry, Shaquille O’Neal and Naomi Osaka, among others. He also had close ties to U.S. regulators and government officials, many of whom he donated to.","entities":["SBF","SBF’s trial","Series C round","Gisele Bündchen","Shaquille O’Neal","Naomi Osaka","SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here?","Miami Heat","government officials","TechCrunch","FTX","Major League Baseball","Tom Brady","U.S. regulators","Steph Curry"],"facts":["SBF Trial: The latest updates from the FTX collapse’s courtroom drama -MENTIONS-> SBF","SBF, riding high on FTX, reportedly offered $5B to Trump to cancel President re-run -MENTIONS-> SBF","Looking for a book to read? Here are 14 tips for October -MENTIONS-> SBF","SBF -SAID-> effective altruist","Dan Held -SAID-> SBF"]}

{"title":"CEO David Baszucki’s mission to make Roblox a billion-player platform (The Verge, 2023-10-12T14:01:00+00:00)","text":"CEO David Baszucki’s mission to make Roblox a billion-player platform (The Verge, 2023-10-12T14:01:00+00:00)
Jay Peters: Hi. Jay Peters with The Verge. You mentioned walled gardens in terms of PlayStation and Xbox, but I kind of feel like Roblox is its own walled garden. We see lots of other shared virtual experience apps like Fortnite or Meta’s Horizon Worlds. Is there any chance or any thinking on some kind of interoperability between all that stuff?

DB: I think there are two types of interoperability. One would just be on valuable items like a pair of shoes from Nike and whether the NFT supports the interchange. That may not be a 3D graphical technical spec; that may be a little bit more of a cloud ownership spec. I think that this genre is evolving so quickly to network hundreds of people to have realistic 3D. Are my shoes ultimately made of leather? Do they actually bend and flex? The technology is going to go so quickly here that any 3D interchange is going to be almost like a five-year-old file format.","entities":["Xbox","Meta","Nike","David Baszucki","Roblox","CEO David Baszucki’s mission to make Roblox a billion-player platform","Jay Peters","Horizon Worlds","interoperability","NFT","Fortnite","PlayStation","The Verge"],"facts":["Video games in 2023: Acquisitions, layoffs, unions -MENTIONS-> Xbox","Mary Jane in Marvel’s Spider-Man 2 Is a Disguised Superhero, in a Good Way -MENTIONS-> Xbox","Sarah Michelle Gellar hits out at Roblox after her son’s account gets hacked -MENTIONS-> Xbox","Microsoft Activision: What does deal mean for gamers? -MENTIONS-> Xbox","Xbox -MENTIONS-> mobile market"]}

