Still, the CPC network may be able to extract some ‘quick win’ concessions from Meta — such as requiring it to amend how it presents the available ‘Hobson’s choice’ to users. Meta could also potentially face pressure to lower the subscription fee to make it more more affordable for users to deny tracking. (Just spitballing here but imagine if it were offering a choice of tracking ads vs paying €1 a year not to be tracked which wouldn’t look so evidently self-serving.)","entities":["Meta","TechCrunch","European consumer groups band together to fight Meta’s self-serving ad-free sub — branding it ‘unfair’ and ‘illegal’","BEUC","CPC network","user reporting and disclosure requirements","ads/sponsored content","digital coins and virtual gifts","European consumer groups","TikTok","ad-free subscription"],"facts":["Meta -MENTIONS-> Al-Aqsa Mosque","Meta -MENTIONS-> WhatsApp","Meta -MENTIONS-> Instagram Stories","Meta -MENTIONS-> Palestine","Meta -MENTIONS-> Colombia"]}

